sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor CU as Customer
    actor CS as CS Agent
    participant UI as Returns Console
    participant EL as Eligibility Engine
    participant RS as Returns Service
    participant IV as Inventory
    participant BA as Bosta Adapter
    participant SP as Shopify
    participant FE as Financial Engine

    Note over CU,FE: Requirement 5 - IN-HOUSE exchange.<br/>Scenario 4: Exchange request -> Confirm Exchange (CS) -> Ready-To-Pick -> Under Return (3PL) -> Returned (WH)<br/>1,612 exchange-tagged items in 7 months.<br/>"Size Issue - Exchange Created" is the top driver.

    CU->>UI: request exchange (wrong size)
    UI->>EL: check eligibility + vendor allows exchange
    EL-->>UI: eligible

    CS->>UI: select replacement variant (size L)
    UI->>IV: is replacement variant in stock?

    alt replacement available
        IV-->>UI: reserved
    else replacement out of stock
        IV-->>UI: unavailable
        CS->>UI: offer alternative variant or convert to refund
        Note right of UI: "Size Issue - Returned (No Exchange)"<br/>occurs 1,050x. Making stock visible<br/>at request time is what converts<br/>those into retained revenue.
    end

    CS->>UI: Confirm Exchange
    UI->>RS: createReturnRequest(type = exchange)
    RS->>RS: INSERT RETURN_REQUESTS + RETURN_ITEMS + EXCHANGES
    RS->>RS: original item status -> Ready-To-Pick

    par reverse leg
        RS->>BA: create reverse pickup AWB (collect original)
        BA-->>RS: reverse tracking number
        RS->>RS: status -> Under Return
    and forward leg
        RS->>SP: create replacement order (linked to original)
        SP-->>RS: replacement order id
        RS->>BA: create forward AWB for replacement item
        Note right of BA: Bosta supports collect-and-deliver<br/>in one visit where the zone allows -<br/>the adapter uses it when available.
    end

    RS->>FE: value the exchange

    Note over FE: The replacement item CARRIES the original<br/>financial snapshot. Revenue is not<br/>recognised twice - the exchange is a<br/>fulfilment substitution, not a new sale.

    FE->>FE: link replacement item -> original snapshot
    FE->>FE: post only the DELTA (price difference,<br/>extra shipping) as new ledger entries

    alt customer pays a price difference
        FE->>SP: charge difference via Paymob link
    else refund a price difference
        FE->>FE: create REFUND for the delta only
    end

    BA->>RS: original received at warehouse
    RS->>RS: QC receipt -> exchange closed

    RS->>UI: update vendor scorecard (exchange rate)
    Note right of UI: Exchange rate per vendor feeds<br/>Requirement 10 - Vendor Score Card.
